{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "properties": {
  "note": "Kapurbawdi to Dhamankar Naka (Phase 1, built): from the station north of the curve onto Ghodbunder Road, OpenStreetMap's Line 5 tracks (ODbL; scripts/data/line5-kapurbawdi-osm.json); then derived from MMRDA's alignment file for Line 5 (https://mmrda.maharashtra.gov.in/sites/default/files/2025-03/metro_line-5.kml), which gives the corridor as a polygon about 50 m wide; the centre line runs midway between its two sides (verified). Past Dhamankar Naka, Phase 2, Phase 3 and the Line 5A spur follow MMRDA's civil tenders of Oct 2026 (CA-317, CA-318, CA-314): the route is traced from the key plan in the tender drawings and placed on the map with the station coordinates the plan sheets print; the stretches where the road flyover and the metro share one structure follow the road centre line in OpenStreetMap (reported; scripts/data/line5-tender-route-2026.geojson, built by scripts/line5-tenders/). Simplified to about 1 m by scripts/build-alignment-line5.py.",
